      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>1.1 threats of harm – Expressing intent, willingness or desire to harm an individual woman or group of women. This could include, but is not limited to: physical, sexual, emotional or privacy-based forms of harm.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Women are targeted online with threats and fantasies of sexual violence, with perpetrators often remaining anonymous. Cyber harassment and bullying can involve threats of violence within a persistent, repeated course of conduct directed at a specific person, designed to cause severe emotional distress and often fear of physical harm.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
