    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID67",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_6eaae8ef8516bdd9f067a960__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks – Expressing strong negative sentiment against women, such as disgust or hatred. This can be through direct description of the speaker’s subjective emotions, baseless accusations, or the use of gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and gender-based insults.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Online gender-based hate speech includes digitally posted or shared content that is hateful towards women and girls because of their gender, alone or in combination with factors such as race, disability, sexuality, religion or profession. It also includes content that spreads, incites, promotes or justifies such hatred. Violent content can portray women and girls as sexual objects or targets of violence, can be shared privately or publicly, and is often directed at women in public-facing roles.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
