      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.2 aggressive and emotive attacks – Expressing strong negative sentiment against women, such as disgust or hatred. This can be through direct description of the speaker’s subjective emotions, baseless accusations, or the use of gendered slurs, gender-based profanities and gender-based insults.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist hate speech expresses contempt toward people based on sex or gender and includes expressions that spread, incite, promote, or justify hatred based on sex. Its forms include victim blaming and re-victimisation, slut-shaming, body-shaming, sharing sexual images without consent, brutal and sexualised threats of death, rape and violence, and offensive comments about appearance, sexuality, sexual orientation or gender roles. It also includes false compliments or supposed jokes that use humour to humiliate and ridicule the target. Many targeted women do not report sexist hate speech, so its extent remains partly hidden.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
