      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>2.3 dehumanising attacks and overt sexual objectification – Derogating women by comparing them to non-human entities such as vermin, disease or refuse, or overtly reducing them to sexual objects.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Racist and sexist hate speech against Black women in politics includes dehumanising comparisons to non-human animals such as “monkey” and “ape,” alongside racial and sexist slurs and calls for mob attacks, lynching, and death by STI. Far-right groups have also used public billboards to demand that a Black woman parliamentarian be “whitened with bleach and burned alive.” This abuse combines dehumanising subhuman framing, sexualised degradation, and incitement to violent elimination.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
