        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.2 immutable gender differences and gender stereotypes – Asserting immutable, natural or otherwise essential differences between men and women. In some cases, this could be in the form of using women’s traits to attack men. Most sexist jokes will fall into this category.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexism is tied to beliefs about the fundamental nature of women and men and the roles they should play in society. Sexist assumptions manifest as gender stereotypes that can rank one gender as superior to another, and this hierarchical thinking may be conscious and hostile or unconscious bias. These stereotypes and attitudes contribute to inequalities women experience, including under-representation in decision-making roles, exclusion from certain economic sectors, primary responsibility for unpaid care work, lower pay than men, and disproportionate subjection to gender-based violence.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
