        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.3 backhanded gendered compliments – Ostensibly complimenting women, but actually belittling or implying their inferiority. This could include, but is not limited to: reduction of women’s value to their attractiveness or sexual desirability, or implication that women are innately frail, helpless or weak.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Gender stereotypes reinforce sexism, and gender stereotypes and inherent biases shape norms, behaviour and expectations among men and boys, leading to sexist acts. Sexism disproportionately affects women and girls and creates barriers to their empowerment. Everyday sexism forms part of a continuum of violence linked to violence against women and girls, creating a climate of intimidation, fear, discrimination, exclusion and insecurity that limits opportunities and freedom.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
