      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.4 condescending explanations or unwelcome advice – Offering unsolicited or patronising advice to women on topics and issues they know more about (known as ‘mansplaining’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexist assumptions about women and men can take the form of gender stereotypes that rank one gender as superior to another. This hierarchical thinking can be consciously hostile or operate as unconscious bias. Women are particularly affected by sexism, and sexist attitudes, practices and behaviour contribute to gender inequalities.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
