    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID122",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_c0703fee9a50b64d4954d390__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">What is sexism?\n\nSexism is linked to beliefs around the fundamental nature of women and men and the roles they should play in society. Sexist assumptions about women and men, which manifest themselves as gender stereotypes, can rank one gender as superior to another. Such hierarchical thinking can be conscious and hostile, or it can be unconscious, manifesting itself as unconscious bias. Sexism can touch everyone, but women are particularly affected.\n\nDespite legal frameworks set up across the EU to prevent discrimination and promote equality, women are still under-represented in decision-making roles, left out of certain sectors of the economy, primarily responsible for unpaid care work, paid less than men and disproportionately subject to gender-based violence. Sexist attitudes, practices and behaviour contribute to these inequalities.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexism involves beliefs about the fundamental nature of women and men and the roles they should play in society. Sexist assumptions manifest as gender stereotypes that can rank one gender as superior to another, and this hierarchical thinking can be conscious and hostile or unconscious, appearing as unconscious bias. Women are particularly affected by sexism, and sexist attitudes, practices and behaviour contribute to inequalities, including women being under-represented in decision-making roles and left out of certain sectors of the economy.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_c0703fee9a50b64d4954d390__deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017",
        "QuestionType": "MC",
        "Selector": "SAVR",
        "SubSelector": "TX",
