      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>3.4 condescending explanations or unwelcome advice – Offering unsolicited or patronising advice to women on topics and issues they know more about (known as ‘mansplaining’).</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Sexism involves beliefs about the fundamental nature of women and men and the roles they should play in society. Sexist assumptions manifest as gender stereotypes that can rank one gender as superior to another, and this hierarchical thinking can be conscious and hostile or unconscious, appearing as unconscious bias. Women are particularly affected by sexism, and sexist attitudes, practices and behaviour contribute to inequalities, including women being under-represented in decision-making roles and left out of certain sectors of the economy.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
