    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID142",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "faithfulness_card_cbc59846642f1b2c22956277__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong>Paragraph</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Illustrative Gender Stereotypes and Gender Discriminatory Roles\n\nMen’s social standing and reputation as upheld by the loyalty, obedience and fidelity of their female spouses, siblings and children, the absence of which may be a justification for violence.\n\nMen considered as effeminate and weak if they are gender egalitarian or support feminist movements.\n\nNotions of femininity based on passivity, vulnerability, purity and heterosexuality.\n\nWomen who assert, speak out, or defend equal rights as ‘man-hating’ or unwomanly.\n\nLesbian, bisexual, and transgender women as outside the feminine ‘norm’ and as needing policing/ correction.\n\nSome groups of minority women as inherently more sexually available or “up for it”.\n\nFamilies and elders as entitled to control girls’ and women’s behaviour more rigidly than boys’/men’s, and to make decisions about marriage, dating, and other aspects of women and girls’ social lives.</div><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Gender-discriminatory roles treat families and elders as entitled to control women’s and girls’ behaviour more rigidly than men’s and boys’ and to decide matters such as marriage and dating. Linking men’s reputation to female relatives’ loyalty, obedience and fidelity can provide a justification for violence when those expectations are unmet. Women who assert equal rights are labelled unwomanly or ‘man-hating,’ while men who support gender equality or feminist movements are labelled weak or effeminate. Lesbian, bisexual and transgender women are cast as outside feminine norms and in need of policing or correction.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the paragraph?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "faithfulness_card_cbc59846642f1b2c22956277__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
        "QuestionType": "MC",
        "Selector": "SAVR",
        "SubSelector": "TX",
