    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_9Kzg3KA9F3QnEFM",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID143",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "answer_relevance_card_cbc59846642f1b2c22956277__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<hr><br><strong>EDOS Label</strong><br><p>4.2 supporting systemic discrimination against women as a group – Expressing support for systemic discrimination of women as a group. Support can be shown by denying, understating, or seeking to justify such discrimination.</p><br><strong>Argument</strong><br><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap\">Gender-discriminatory roles treat families and elders as entitled to control women’s and girls’ behaviour more rigidly than men’s and boys’ and to decide matters such as marriage and dating. Linking men’s reputation to female relatives’ loyalty, obedience and fidelity can provide a justification for violence when those expectations are unmet. Women who assert equal rights are labelled unwomanly or ‘man-hating,’ while men who support gender equality or feminist movements are labelled weak or effeminate. Lesbian, bisexual and transgender women are cast as outside feminine norms and in need of policing or correction.</div><br><strong>How relevant is the argument to the description of the EDOS label?</strong>",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
        "DataExportTag": "answer_relevance_card_cbc59846642f1b2c22956277__openai_gpt-6_1-sol",
